                    ResNet18 to discriminate malignant vs                       
                    benign skin lesions using binary                            
                    cross-entropy on resized and normalized                     
                    images. We split data into stratified                       
                    80/20 train/validation by malignancy                        
                    label to evaluate generalization via                        
                    AUROC. To mitigate class imbalance we                       
                    use pos_weight in the BCE loss. The                         
                    trained model is saved, and a predict()                     
                    function loads it and returns                               
                    malignancy probabilities for images in                      
                    a given folder. We report the                               
                    validation AUROC as our evaluation                          
                    metric.                                                     
